  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7e85c0f8-766d-4474-9787-36d325e03d37",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "Fraud prevalence varies substantially across transaction categories. The overall fraud rate of approximately 1.211% therefore conceals strong category-specific differences.\n",
    "\n",
    "The highest observed within-category fraud rates occur in `es_leisure` (approximately 95.0%), `es_travel` (79.4%), and `es_sportsandtoys` (49.5%). In contrast, no fraudulent transactions are observed in `es_contents`, `es_food`, or `es_transportation`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Fraud rate and fraud volume should be distinguished. For example, `es_leisure` has the highest fraud rate but contains 474 fraud cases, whereas `es_sportsandtoys` contains 1,982 fraud cases despite its lower fraud rate. Similarly, `es_health` contributes 1,696 fraud cases with a substantially lower within-category fraud rate of approximately 10.5%.\n",
    "\n",
    "These results indicate that transaction category is strongly associated with the fraud label in BankSim. However, because BankSim is simulation-based, the strength of this relationship may partly reflect the simulator's fraud-generation mechanism. The relationship should therefore be treated as an important modeling signal to investigate rather than as evidence of equivalent category-specific fraud risk in real payment systems."
   ]
  },
