    "This illustrates the distinction between fraud prevalence and fraud volume. For example, `leisure` has the highest within-category fraud rate (approximately 95.0%) but contributes only about 6.58% of all fraud cases because the category contains relatively few transactions. In contrast, `health` has a much lower fraud rate (approximately 10.51%) but contributes approximately 23.56% of all fraud cases because of its larger transaction volume.\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus, category-level fraud behavior should be evaluated using both within-category fraud rates and contributions to the total number of fraud cases."
