  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b3840006-d1a6-441c-a9ea-538bfc8c7350",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Temporal Structure of the Fraud Label\n",
    "\n",
    "A notable structural property is that every one of the 180 simulation steps contains exactly 40 fraudulent transactions, giving a total of 7,200 fraud cases.\n",
    "\n",
    "Consequently, variation in the step-level fraud rate is driven by variation in the total number of transactions per step rather than by variation in the number of observed fraud cases. The correlation between transaction volume and step-level fraud percentage is approximately -0.9934, but this strong negative association is largely mechanical because the numerator of the fraud-rate calculation is fixed at 40 for every step.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, a decline in step-level fraud percentage should not be interpreted as evidence that the underlying number of fraud cases decreases over time or that higher transaction volume causes lower fraud risk. This structure is also relevant when designing the later validation strategy because the temporal behavior partly reflects the BankSim simulation mechanism."
   ]
  },
